WEBVTT

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.630
than the north end of a southbound moose out there.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:58.620
Rhys Bannon?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.520
I've been waiting for you.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.990
We've been waiting for you to start our supper.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.010
I hope Yak will be satisfactory.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.050
Gentlemen.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.170
But Troy Lee, I thought Yak were endangered.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.010
This high in the Himalayas.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.630
We are all endangered.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.580
These yaks are domesticated, of course.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.810
Tell that to the yak I wrote in on.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.420
Though I must admit, that smells pretty good.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:29.800
Benton.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.360
Race, it's good to see you again.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.120
And you, Prasad. It's been a long time.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.540
Only if you perceive time as a line, Vinton.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.420
I prefer to view it as a series of now points.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.920
Heck of a location you chose, Prasad.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.820
I didn't want to disappoint you, Race.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.160
It isn't often that we get together to compare notes on our recent adventures.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.300
Above all people, Prasad,

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.630
you know that phenomenology is a little more than simple adventuring.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.980
Well, it looks like the satellite's over.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:12.200
ahead. Time to check in with Johnny. Your signal's pretty weak, Pop. I can barely hear you. It's an

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:20.360
six hours. No problem. Don't worry about the three of us. Everything's cool here. Did you hear it,

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:29.980
Lorenzo? Everything's cool? No. The sound of opportunity knocking. Haji's pulse rates return.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.230
He's turning to normal. He's leaving the astral plane.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.600
Come on, Haji. Tell us what it's like out there.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.950
The astral plane? The mind is everywhere and nowhere.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.650
It is empty of thought, good or wicked.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.520
There is no trace of self-awareness. You simply float.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.240
Yeah, great, okay. But what's it look like?

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.010
It is impossible to describe the indescribable.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.950
Nothing's impossible, Haji. There are only possibilities waiting to be discovered.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.220
You sound more like Haji every day.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:04:59.970
I'm talking.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.420
We're talking about Quest World, Jess.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.560
We'll use the Quest World system to tap into Haji's brain waves.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:10.450
Then the Quest World screens will show us Haji's view of the astral plane.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.950
You are downloading my brain into Quest World?

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:14.390
I am dumbfounded.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.830
Quest World, log on. Subject, Haji.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.540
Okay, Haji. The ball's in your court.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:33.500
It's working.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:35.440
Asty.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.230
Haji's mind is driving the system.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.000
No wonder he couldn't describe it.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:51.920
No offense, Prasad, but this yak meet is tougher than my 30-year-old combat boot.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.260
I'll take that as a compliment, Grace.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.880
By the way, Benton, why did you wish to meet three weeks earlier than we had previously scheduled?

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.400
What are you talking about, Prasad?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.220
You sent me a message changing the dates.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:06.180
Not so.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.640
You sent me an email requesting that we make it for this month instead of next.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.540
I sent no such communique.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:13.900
Hold on now.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.140
If neither of you changed the dates, then who did?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:25.210
Verify the weather patterns over the Himalayas and positions of communication satellites.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.780
If my calculations were correct, then I'm sure.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.220
and Bannum will be completely isolated in those godforsaken mountains.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:36.850
Hmm, that's strange.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.130
I'm picking up a unique energy pattern in Quest World.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.890
It's very similar to Alpha Brainwaves.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.120
That's investigating.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.140
Mr. Surt, we're three miles off from the Quest compound.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.580
Well, then you know what to do.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:27.660
Don't sound right evil.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.140
We better get Hodge out of there.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.600
Time to come back, Haji.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:32.590
Haji?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:33.580
Haji?

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.720
His heart rate's down, Jess.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.080
We better check his brain way back.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:38.440
Right.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.280
He's in deep alpha-stack.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.820
It's Jeremiah Surd.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.640
Power up the quest world, Jess.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:56.820
No buts.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.780
Haji's gonna lose his mind literally if we don't do something now.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:02.920
Quest World, log on.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:04.960
Subject, Johnny Quest.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:05.760
Countdown.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:09.410
Six, five, four, three.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.750
Program any of this.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:48.410
His brain slowly frying away to nothing.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.200
Of course, could stop the process.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.460
There's a price, right?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:55.470
Hours.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.480
I want your father and Ray Spannon here in five minutes!

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:08.660
Or little Haji will be on the menu tomorrow as the vegetable de jure.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:09.920
But I...

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:10.190
No.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.070
Wait, wait.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.650
I've grown tired of you.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.830
Johnny Quest logging off.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:28.070
Everything is going as planned.

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:29.970
With my disposal of...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.570
their fathers in the himalayas little johnny and jesse will have no choice as soon as they both

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:42.980
enter quest world the quest compound will be ours for the taking we are ready to move in as soon as

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:49.020
you give the word jeremiah but i don't get it boss what's the big deal what do they got that we need

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:56.200
i don't expect you to comprehend lorenzo your mind is as childlike as the quest they have no concept

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.980
to the powers of Questworld and are therefore unworthy of its position.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:06.890
Once you and Julia destroy their equipment and files, I can lock them out of Quest World forever.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:11.310
Leaving me the undisputed controller of cyberspace.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:13.440
...up a creek.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.200
Yeah, but we still have a paddle, Jess.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.960
Two, actually. Our dads.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:19.100
They're on the other side of the planet.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.340
No. Quest World is its own reality. Why can't we just impersonate them?

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.210
Because there are just two of us.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.320
And we've always had one golden rule.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.980
There has to be someone on the outside to monitor.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:43.380
address it's all or nothing you're right the rules changed hasn't it move it give me a hand here

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:59.740
release it sir julia here

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.000
We are underway.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.820
And so am I.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:04.390
Quest World log on.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.250
Subject, Jeremiah CERT.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:09.940
Running out of time.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.000
CERT only gave us five minutes.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:14.020
Tell me news, not history, Jess.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:15.780
Quest Compound.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:19.240
Defense systems up and running with one addition.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:21.360
I call it a CERT Protector.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.240
Quest World log on.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.880
Subjects, Johnny Quest and Jesse Bannon.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.110
Going hot.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:31.660
Three, two...

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.840
We'll synthesize Ray's and Dad's voices.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.690
Sir will never know the difference.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:44.310
Welcome to my playground, gentlemen.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.060
I'm so glad you could attend my little bar.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.300
He tells me you better get out of here.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:10.040
Let's move! There it is. Quest.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:13.640
Those kids locked in the Quest world.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:16.040
Everything is ours for the taking.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.020
Move, Johnny.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.600
Doesn't look good.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.290
Remember the surge protector I programmed earlier?

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:29.970
It's good to see you, Madame Fournier.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.980
Would you care to begin?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:31.720
Really?

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:36.140
I believe you have identified a mysterious emanation at the mouth of the Zambezi?

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:37.940
You are quite right, Madame Fournier.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:42.450
But it would be more correct for us to wait for Mr. Prasad before we proceed.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:46.920
Programming.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:50.810
Slowly frying away to nothing.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:57.040
Welcome to my playground, gentlemen.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.400
A vegetable dijon.

